</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted our experiments on three models, including LLaMA2-7b-chat <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, LLaMA3-8b-instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and Mistral-7b-instruct-v0.2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Their maximum context length ranges from 4k to 32k. LLaMA2-7b employs MHA, while LLaMA3-8b and Mistral-7b utilize GQA with <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}=8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}=4</annotation></semantics></math>. All models’ <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=32</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the model’s knowledge and reasoning capabilities on <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LongBench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, which contains 16 long-context knowledge intensive subsets covering 6 tasks including multi-document question answering (QA), single-document QA, summarization, few-show learning, synthetic tasks and code, with the length of most tasks ranging from <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>k to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math>k. We also evaluate our method on <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Needle-in-a-Haystack</span> task <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Briakou et al., 2023</a>)</cite> to test the long-context retrieval ability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We select <span id="S4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Pyramidinfer</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> and <span id="S4.SS1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PyramidKV</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cai et al., 2024</a>)</cite> as baselines, both of which compress the KV cache based on token eviction method and allocate pyramid shaped KV cache cross layers.</p>
<table id="S4.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{\begin{aligned} r_{1}^{\lambda}&amp;=\frac{\sum_{j=0}^{h_{g}-1}(|K_{\lambda}^{j,r}|+|V_{\lambda}^{j,r}|)}{\sum_{j=0}^{h_{g}-1}(|K_{j}^{i}|+|V_{j}^{i}|)}\\
r_{2}^{\lambda}&amp;=\frac{|C^{\lambda}_{K}\cup C^{\lambda}_{V}|}{\sum_{j=0}^{h_{g}}(|K_{j,r}^{\lambda}|+|V_{j,r}^{\lambda}|)}\\
r_{3}^{\lambda}&amp;=\frac{1}{d_{h}}\left(d_{h}+\frac{\mathrm{int\_bit}}{\mathrm{key\_bit+1}}\right)\\
\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>bit</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>key</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>bit</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{\begin{aligned} r_{1}^{\lambda}&amp;=\frac{\sum_{j=0}^{h_{g}-1}(|K_{\lambda}^{j,r}|+|V_{\lambda}^{j,r}|)}{\sum_{j=0}^{h_{g}-1}(|K_{j}^{i}|+|V_{j}^{i}|)}\\
r_{2}^{\lambda}&amp;=\frac{|C^{\lambda}_{K}\cup C^{\lambda}_{V}|}{\sum_{j=0}^{h_{g}}(|K_{j,r}^{\lambda}|+|V_{j,r}^{\lambda}|)}\\
r_{3}^{\lambda}&amp;=\frac{1}{d_{h}}\left(d_{h}+\frac{\mathrm{int\_bit}}{\mathrm{key\_bit+1}}\right)\\
\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\lambda}=r_{1}^{\lambda}\times r_{2}^{\lambda}\times r_{3}^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\lambda}=r_{1}^{\lambda}\times r_{2}^{\lambda}\times r_{3}^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E15Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\lambda=0}^{m-1}r^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{\lambda=0}^{m-1}r^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We use the reserve ratio <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to measure the compression intensity. We define <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> as the reserve ratio for <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer, which is co-determined by <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reserve ratio of eviction method, <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reserve ratio of replacement method, and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,3}</annotation></semantics></math>, serves as the <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dtype</span> convert ratio
since we store <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">int</span> type index and <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">float</span> type magnitude for each key and value. The calculation is given by Formura <a href="#S4.E15" title="In 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SpindleKV: A Novel KV Cache Reduction Method Balancing Both Shallow and Deep Layers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>. <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\lambda}=r_{1}^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\lambda}=r_{1}^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> for pyramidinfer and PyramidKV, and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}=h</annotation></semantics></math> if a repeat operation is conducted before eviction. We record <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for every input when evaluating on <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LongBench</span> to ensure their precision.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
